# Load the one saved character and quit straight back out, saving again on
# the way. tools/check_v1_full_roundtrip.sh drives this once per fixpoint
# generation: quick-quit's save writes the next file of its save2-vs-save3
# field comparison. No gameplay happens in between on purpose -- any turn
# taken here would make the generations legitimately different beyond the
# script's documented volatile-field allowlist.
#
#   tools/headless.sh tools/keys/loadsave.keys 1
#
# The run directory must already hold exactly one save in save/ (the check
# copies one in). With one save present the load menu is deterministic.

@expect "Initial Choices"
@choose "Restore a Saved Game"
@expect "Choose a character:"
a

@dump:loaded

@quit
